    v2-0-RC3/resources/xml/types-include.xml
    at commit 418a8f6.

  LICENSE, the text of CC BY-ND 4.0 as that repository publishes it.

These copies are outside this repository's Apache License, and this project
claims no right over them.

Nothing else here repeats or adapts FIX's text. What the schema takes from
FIX is the element and attribute names and the structure, which a message
schema must use to work with SBE at all. Copyright protects the way FIX
expressed its specification, not the methods, procedures and facts it
describes, and CC BY-ND 4.0 restricts nothing that copyright does not (its
section 8(a)).

The project nevertheless takes the stricter reading that European law
allows (Infopaq, C-5/08), under which even a short extract can be protected
when it shows its author's own choices. Every title, description and comment
was written from what the element does, in the project's own words, not by
rewording FIX's sentences. tests/test_own_words.py finds any run of four
words shared with the documentation in the XSDs, and the same check was run
by hand against the specification's text, which stays out of this repository.
The specification remains the authority on what SBE says.

The site fixtrading.org has terms of its own, which bar automated copying of
its content. Nothing here was taken from that site, and the upstream watch
reads only GitHub.

The schema's description slot holds whatever its user writes into it. Fill
it only with text you have the right to use. The Apache License of this
repository does not cover FIX's text.

